  ],
  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A wheel of radius R and mass M is placed at the bottom of a fixed step of height R as shown in the figure. A constant force is continuously applied on the surface of the wheel so that it just climbs the step without slipping. Consider the torque <math><mi>τ</mi></math> about an axis normal to the plane of the paper passing through the point Q. Which of the following options is/are correct?<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/lutgkulkqbltyxuimlbgmsfbvxuczjxoryrrecjcnmrjddyrsk.jpeg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "A0pLZ",
      "text": "If the force is applied normal to the circumference at point  <math><mi>X</mi></math>  then  <math><mi>τ</mi></math>  is constant",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "65uXs",
      "text": "If the force is applied tangentially at point S then  <math><mi>τ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math>  but the wheel never climbs the step",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p6GcN",
      "text": "If the force is applied normal to the circumference at point P then <math><mi>&tau;</mi></math> is zero",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "19fT4",
      "text": "If the force is applied at point P tangentially then  <math><mi>τ</mi></math>  decreases continuously as the wheel climbs",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(i) is incorrect.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/11_solu_phy_pa_2.jpg\"/></p><p>If force is applied normal to surface at point <math><mi>X</mi></math></p><p><math><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mi> </mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></math></p><p>Thus <math><mi>τ</mi></math> depends on <math><mi>θ</mi></math> and it is not constant</p><p>(ii) is incorrect</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/11_solu_phy_pa_2_1.jpg\"/></p><p>If force applied tangentially at S</p><p><math><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>R</mi><mi> </mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>But it will climb as mentioned in question.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/11_solu_phy_pa_2_2.jpg\"/></p><p>If force is applied normal to surface at P then line of action of force will pass from Q and thus <math><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>(iv) is incorrect.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/11_solu_phy_pa_2_3.jpg\"/></p><p>If force is applied at P tangentially the <math><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
